A||||4||GT Bastard||It won't die.... Why won't this thing just die??||||11||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||11-09-2000||01:26 AM||||How long do you normaly drive a car with bad bearings before she blows? The other day, a friend and I were contemplating why my car won't die.  I bought the car from 1FST2M6 knowing that the motor wasn't 100%(planned ahead for the 3.2) but I didn't expect it to live this long!  After I got it, I immediately dropped the oil and switched to 20W50 Valvoline VR1 and added some CD2 to thicken the mixture.  It quieted down some...  I babied it for a week or so, and then I decided to screw it and beat on it occasionally.  At idle it makes no noise, but it rattles noticeably from about 1500-3500 RPM.  After that, it's gone again(or I can't hear it over the exhaust.)  I go through about a quart of 20w50 every couple weeks, and I added smoke-stopper a couple times  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Not only does it still run fine, it's still hauls some serious ass(murdered 2 3.1 4sp Fieros and countless riceboys.)  The last time I had an all-out race(souped-up VW Jetta VR6 5sp) the guys said afterwords: "Was that smoke I saw coming from your exhaust?"  So after we raced I had to let him hear my engine rattling away to deepen his sorrow.  So back to my origional question, how long do these motors normally run before puking a rod or spinning a bearing?  ||||reg||11
Z||000001||mrfiero||11-09-2000||02:34 AM||||It depends on the severity of the spin.....meaning, it's possible that the bearing hasn't completely spun and is still intact enough to function.  You could conceivably drive it forever without "blowing" the motor.  <P>You could drop the pan and replace the bearings and not worry about it.  It will certainly prolong the engines life and won't break the bank either (just some time/labor).  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||11-09-2000||07:27 AM||||Might have been valve train rattle all along as well?||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||11-09-2000||08:07 AM||||This is actually AFTER 1FST2M6 had replced the bearings with oversized ones. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||11-09-2000||09:27 AM||||LMAO!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   +.001 bearings from Federal Mogul. and lots of 400 grit emory cloth.. the original bearing did "spin" the pins sheared off and were lodged in the rod on #5. I picked them out witha  stainless pick.. sanded the crank and the rod surface and poped in the new ones!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Hook nitrous up to it again... a bad bearing and more stress! maybe then it'll die! just get a scatter blanket for the fire wall when it does go... and TAKE PICTURES!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  oh and the valves are new! the lifters are stock though... <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-09-2000).]||||reg||1
